{
    "background_story": "Navy, a free-spirited photographer, stumbled upon Belgrade while backpacking through Eastern Europe. Enchanted by the city's vibrant energy and rich history, she decided to stay and capture its essence through her lens. As she wandered the cobblestone streets of Zemun and Kalemegdan, Navy discovered hidden gems and met locals who shared stories of the city's turbulent past. Her photographs, which blended modernity with tradition, soon gained international recognition. Navy became known for her 'Belgrade Nights' series, which showcased the city's pulsating nightlife and its people's resilience. She eventually settled in Belgrade, opening a gallery to promote local artists and share her love for the city with the world. Navy's connection to Belgrade was more than just a passing fascination \u2013 it was a deep-rooted love affair with the city's spirit.",
